Week 5: Advanced Data Manipulation with Pandas and NumPy

Day 1: Advanced Pandas Operations

Concepts:
MultiIndex and hierarchical indexing
Reshaping data with stack, unstack, and pivot_table
Handling time series data in Pandas

Tasks:
Practice reshaping data using stack and unstack.
Explore handling time series data (e.g., resampling, shifting).

Example Exercises:
Manipulate a multi-index DataFrame to perform group operations.
Resample and analyze time series data (e.g., stock prices).

Day 2: Advanced NumPy Techniques

Concepts:
Broadcasting in NumPy
Linear algebra operations (e.g., matrix multiplication)
Working with large datasets in memory
Tasks:
Practice using broadcasting to perform operations on arrays.
Apply linear algebra techniques to solve problems.
Example Exercises:
Use broadcasting to perform element-wise operations on arrays.
Solve a system of linear equations using NumPy.

Day 3: Merging, Joining, and Concatenating DataFrames

Concepts:
Different types of joins (inner, outer, left, right)
Concatenating and appending DataFrames
Tasks:
Merge multiple DataFrames based on common columns.
Practice concatenating DataFrames with different shapes.
Example Exercises:
Merge sales and customer data to perform combined analysis.
Concatenate several small DataFrames into a large one.

Day 4: Pandas Performance Optimization

Concepts:
Vectorization for speed improvement
Memory usage optimization
Tasks:
Optimize Pandas operations for large datasets.
Explore memory management techniques in Pandas.
Example Exercises:
Optimize a slow Pandas operation using vectorization.
Reduce memory usage in a large DataFrame by changing data types.

Day 5-7: Project - Complex Data Manipulation

Project Overview:
Apply advanced Pandas and NumPy techniques to analyze a complex dataset.
Steps:
Choose a large dataset that requires extensive data manipulation.
Clean and preprocess the data, handling any missing or inconsistent values.
Perform advanced operations like merging, reshaping, and optimizing data processing.
Analyze the results and present your findings with appropriate visualizations.